/* =============================================================================
   Theraglee — Playlists: a genre, then a mood, then forty songs.
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   A Premium feature on the member dashboard (dashboard.html#playlists). The
   member picks one of the genres below, then one of the moods, and gets the
   curated list for that pair: forty songs, every one on both Apple Music and
   Spotify. Each list is also a public playlist in Theraglee's Spotify account
   (made by tools/spotify_playlists.mjs), played right on the page. The
   drawing lives in playlists-ui.js; tests/playlists-fixture/check.mjs guards
   this file.

   Shape
     GENRES     [{ key, name, blurb }]              the genres, in the order shown
     MOODS      [{ key, name, blurb, wants }]       the moods, in the order shown
     PLAYLISTS  { [genre.key]: { [mood.key]: { title, blurb, spotify, songs } } }
     spotify    the id of this list's public playlist on Spotify, or '' until
                tools/spotify_playlists.mjs has made it; with an id the tab
                shows a Spotify player, without one it shows links per song
     songs      [[title, artist], ...]              exactly forty per list

   Writing rules
   - Forty songs a list, none repeated within a genre.
   - Well-known releases only, so both services carry them; no live-only
     cuts, no bootlegs, no songs that were ever pulled from streaming.
   - A mood is a place to start from, never a diagnosis: "Low and heavy"
     lists music that keeps someone company, not music about being low.
   - "Angry" gives the feeling somewhere to go; nothing on it glorifies harm.
   - "Lonely" is company: songs about friends, home and showing up for each
     other, not songs that dwell on being alone.
   - "Winding down" is slow and soft, for the last hour before sleep.
   ============================================================================= */

